WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
This one is by popular request so

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.500
'Triumph of the Will' and the cinematic

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:16.680
language of propaganda.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.770
'Triumph of the Will' is not a triumph of film-making.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.190
I just want to lay that out before we even start.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.000
Chances are good that you're familiar

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.070
with 'Triumph of the Will' by reputation

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.740
but have never actually watched it

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.800
beyond referential clips, and a sizable

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.750
portion of that reputation is in its

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.680
value as an advancement of the art of filmmaking.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.960
This is propaganda.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.340
Like, that belief is in and of itself propaganda.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:44.160
Nazi sympathizers spent a lot

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.750
of time between the film's release in

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.079
1935 and the war promoting the idea of

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:52.220
'Triumph of the Will' as an advancement of filmmaking.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.850
It was an intentional message

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:57.270
to promote Nazi state art as superior, to

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.520
suggest that the Nazi mechanism can

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.980
produce better more proficient art than

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.890
the artist the Nazis were busy throwing in jail.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:09.780
It is however not a triumph of filmmaking; it is a triumph of budget.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:14.189
None of the ideas or techniques were new it is simply that no one had previously

00:01:14.189 --> 00:01:18.840
thrown enough money and resources at propaganda on this scale before.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.790
We'll come back to this and develop it in more

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.600
detail, but I want to be upfront with the fact that you should be highly

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.950
suspicious of any messaging surrounding propaganda.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:33.210
ok so vocabulary groundwork: we're going

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:37.640
to make a distinction about what we mean when we say propaganda.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.560
Broadly speaking propaganda is just any goal-driven

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.939
ideological message, and a lot of stuff incidentally falls under that umbrella.

00:01:44.939 --> 00:01:50.820
For example any official message from an activist community meets the literal definition.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:55.320
Signs encouraging you to, like, pick up after your dog.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.250
So the first thing that we need to make note of is the textural difference

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:04.620
between the literal definition of propaganda and how people actually use the word.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:09.599
Contextually propaganda is used derisively, not merely used to describe

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:13.830
the literal characteristics of some text or another, but carries with it a value judgments

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:20.040
with the implicit understanding that propaganda is bad.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.720
Memetically, propaganda represents not just rhetoric but some degree of dishonesty:

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.120
not an attempt to persuade but to deceive.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.300
Not an attempt to inform but to inflame.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:35.160
And even by this metric there's still plenty that qualifies as

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.480
propaganda from white nationalists spreading false statistics about crime

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.880
to corporations trying to paper over the damage they do to bloggers being paid to

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.650
pretend to like a video game.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:51.420
So what we're going to do here is draw a fine line between propaganda and

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:56.310
PROPAGANDA, the distinction being a difference between general propaganda

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:00.848
and propaganda generated by and in service of governments.

00:03:00.848 --> 00:03:03.330
I feel like this is an important distinction to make

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:08.070
because there is a potent contextual difference between, say, the propaganda

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:13.500
tracts and memes spread by hate groups and those spread by the state.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.500
That distinction is order of magnitude.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.019
The sheer reach and spending power at the

00:03:19.019 --> 00:03:21.420
disposal of government is so far beyond

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.970
the scope of even corporations that it's

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.580
a laughable comparison.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:30.700
The US federal government's annual revenue is 3.6 trillion dollars.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.720
The largest corporation in the world, Walmart, sees an annual

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:37.260
revenue of 482 billion dollars.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.800
The 10 largest corporations combined still fall

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.520
almost a trillion dollars short.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:46.440
Global box office revenue comes in around 38

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.510
billion dollars, and Pirates of the

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.160
Caribbean four is ranked as the most

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.820
expensive movie ever made at 378 million

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.830
dollars but on the scope of federal

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.230
budgets, especially those related to the

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.870
military, its budget is a rounding error.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.820
And this isn't even touching on the

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:05.010
power that government have to enact and

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.989
enforce the underlying policies that

00:04:06.989 --> 00:04:09.269
propaganda supports. The point is that

00:04:09.269 --> 00:04:11.549
large, motivated governments can

00:04:11.549 --> 00:04:13.830
effortlessly outspend any other

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:16.169
organized entity on the planet and as a

00:04:16.169 --> 00:04:18.209
result their potential for producing

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:21.000
and disseminating propaganda exist on an

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.100
entirely different plane of operation

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.590
than any other form. When you add in the

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:26.570
potential outcome,

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.910
that propaganda influencing the lives of

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.700
millions or even billions of people, the

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:35.060
stakes to dwarf everything else. It is for

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.710
this reason that we're not going to be

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.870
talking about propaganda in the abstract

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:41.780
but rather is very specific kind of

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.660
propaganda, and with that established

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:47.810
Triumph of the Will

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:54.860
Leni Riefenstahl film Triumph des

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.390
Willens isn't the beginning of

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:58.670
propaganda, it's not even the beginning

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.740
of motion picture propaganda, heck

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.390
it's not even Riefenstahl's first

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:05.660
propaganda film for the Nazis, and i'm

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.940
going to use that as a segue into some

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.210
contextual history. In 1933 Riefenstahl

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.220
documented the annual Nazi Nuremberg

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:15.170
rally in the film Der Sieg Des Glaubens,

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:17.990
Victory of Faith, however that film is

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.340
significantly less well-known.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.790
Filmed at the August 1933 rally celebrating Adolf

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.260
Hitler's appointment to the position of

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.690
chancellor of Germany in January of that

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:31.160
year, the film heavily features founding Nazi Party leader Ernst Röhm.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:35.100
Röhm would be executed a year later in July 1934,

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.480
during the Night of Long Knives, a sweeping ideological purge of

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:42.680
socialist and working-class leadership in the Nazi party, after which it was

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:46.640
ordered that all known copies of Victory of Faith be destroyed as part of an

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:51.500
attempt at rewriting history, erasing Röhm's contributions to the Nazi Party.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:55.040
Due to the high profile of many of the people killed in the purge it was

00:05:55.040 --> 00:06:00.050
impossible to cover up the illegal executions, so Hitler had the cabinet just

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:03.140
make them legal after-the-fact.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:06.410
A month after the purge, August 1934, president

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:10.070
Hindenburg died, and by the middle of August the roles of President and

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.930
Chancellor were merged, making Hitler

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.020
both the head of state and the head of government.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.930
With all of that in mind: a number of very high-profile crimes

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:20.740
followed by a complete restructuring of the government,

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:24.680
in September 1934 Hitler and his party had a vested interest in

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:29.540
reinforcing the perceived legitimacy of the regime and preparing the populace

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:31.400
for the wars that were to come.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.830
And to that end they hired Riefenstahl to make

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.990
a second propaganda documentary at the

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:38.500
now annual Nuremberg rally.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.800
Now let's talk about the language of propaganda.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.180
From a filmmaking perspective propaganda uses all the same grammar as

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.080
any other example of the medium.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:54.460
Contrast, association, implication, these are all

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:57.920
the bread and butter of assembling any visual narrative.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.920
As an example we're going to look at something a little

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:04.090
lighter than Nazis and take a look at Return of the King.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.770
so Return of the King has a scene where

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.870
Denethor has sent Faramir out to die on

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.850
the battlefield and the film cross-cuts

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:11.710
between the battlefield and the hall at the

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.930
palace where Denethor's having dinner. The

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.669
three main things of interest are

00:07:15.669 --> 00:07:19.020
Denethor's eating, Pippin's singing, and Faramir's riding.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:21.970
The film pays particular interest to the squishy

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:24.730
sounds and sloppy process of Denethor's

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:26.830
eating, which when juxtaposed with

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.169
Faramir's suicide mission create thematic

00:07:29.169 --> 00:07:32.140
implications: that Denethor is a careless

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:37.000
sloppy glutton who consumes the lives of the people around him.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.540
He discards his son's life with same grace as he squishes a tomato.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:43.780
Where Pippin and Faramir are highlighted by their faces, their

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:46.120
personages, Denethor is largely viewed

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.090
from severe angles and segmented, reduced

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:51.520
to his hands and his giant consuming

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:54.190
mouth, a visual parallel matched by the

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:55.600
deformed orc Gothmog.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:58.960
Denethor breaks bones and blood runs down his chin,

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:03.220
images which are juxtaposed with the blood streaking the faces of the orcs

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:05.840
preparing to slaughter Faramir's troops.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:12.080
This is all compounded by Pippin's song, which essentially just commentates the contrast as it happens.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.440
The messaging here is pretty straightforward: Denethor is

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:18.200
villainized, a parallel is created between him and the orcs.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.320
Heck, if anything it's ridiculously heavy-handed.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:24.490
The point of this example is to drive home the fact that there really is no

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:28.760
difference in the editing grammar used in one genre versus another.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:31.510
The same process of creating implications, of

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.729
villainizing or lionizing through

00:08:33.729 --> 00:08:36.820
juxtaposed imagery, works the same regardless.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:42.200
Where propaganda diverges is in the nuances of how the message is delivered.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:47.260
One of the sand traps of discussing ideology in cinema is the demand of narrative.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:51.070
Story, at least in the European tradition, requires conflict.

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:54.189
characters must be flawed, they must make mistakes, their

00:08:54.189 --> 00:08:55.810
opponents must get the better of them.

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:59.170
Things in some way shape or form need to

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:02.920
get bad, need to entertain uncertainty.

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:05.230
In Return of the King, a conventional story,

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.750
Denethor's actions must bring Pippin and

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:10.180
Gandalf and Faramir low in order to

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.949
create the tension that will be relieved

00:09:11.949 --> 00:09:15.040
later in the story when the conflict is resolved.

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:16.959
However these basic mechanisms of

00:09:16.959 --> 00:09:18.970
narrative tension are at odds with the

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:21.430
needs of propaganda, because weakness,

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:25.510
failure, and uncertainty are anathema to the propagandist.

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:29.439
The subject of propaganda has no arc but upward, they

00:09:29.439 --> 00:09:32.439
begin strong and stronger, they crush all

00:09:32.439 --> 00:09:34.360
that oppose them, their opposition is

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.460
flimsy and victory is trivial.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:40.160
They win so much that the audience gets tired of all the winning.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:41.709
This is the point.

00:09:41.709 --> 00:09:43.569
Triumph of the Will is no different: it

00:09:43.569 --> 00:09:48.610
is interminable in its assertion of the strength of the Nazi Party, the promise of

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:51.200
victory, and the uselessness of the opposition.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.820
Alright well actually it is a little bit more complicated.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:57.490
See propaganda does still require a worthy

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.649
foe, or more accurately a foe that

00:09:59.649 --> 00:10:02.139
justifies the volume of force that the

00:10:02.139 --> 00:10:04.160
propagandist is trying to rally.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.879
Triumph of the Will, and Nazi ideology in general,

00:10:06.879 --> 00:10:09.339
is obsessed with both the unstoppable

00:10:09.339 --> 00:10:11.559
might of the party and the need for that

00:10:11.559 --> 00:10:13.540
unstoppable might to be levied against

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:17.920
the paradoxically week degenerates who secretly control everything.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:24.200
Umberto Eco in his 1995 essay Ur-Fascism describes this particular ideological quirk:

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:29.559
the followers must feel humiliated by the ostentatious wealth and force of their enemies

00:10:29.559 --> 00:10:33.730
however the followers must be convinced that they can overwhelm the enemy's thus

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:40.420
by a continuous shifting of rhetorical focus the enemies are at the same time too strong and too weak.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:43.560
Fascist governments are condemned to lose wars because they

00:10:43.569 --> 00:10:45.759
are constitutionally incapable of

00:10:45.759 --> 00:10:48.699
objectively evaluating the force of the enemy.

00:10:48.699 --> 00:10:54.189
Let's back up and revisit previous accusation: Triumph of the Will is not a

00:10:54.189 --> 00:10:56.829
triumph of cinema, but of budget. One of

00:10:56.829 --> 00:10:58.569
the central arms of attack that Triumph

00:10:58.569 --> 00:11:00.939
of the Will uses is in its very essence,

00:11:00.939 --> 00:11:04.430
its existence as a grandiose, long,

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:07.430
expensive, complex production. None of the

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.980
filmmaking ideas used were new. putting a

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.470
camera in the back of a car wasn't new.

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:15.529
tracking shots weren't new. low angle

00:11:15.529 --> 00:11:18.200
shots weren't new. aerial shots weren't

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:22.610
new. the only thing new was scope. Every

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:25.010
scene goes on and on for minutes at a

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:25.550
time.

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:27.440
there aren't a few aerial shots, there are

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.930
hundreds. there's not a camera observing

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:32.060
the parade as it passes, there are dozens

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:34.490
of cameras embedded in the very fabric

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:37.700
of the parade. to the modern viewer it

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:40.190
may seem aimless and shoddily paced, with

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:43.700
montages that just go on and on and on

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:46.700
long after the point has been made, but

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.140
that's the point.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.660
it is not merely a demonstration of

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:53.630
presence but of volume. the indulgence of

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:56.660
it, the conspicuous cost, is as much a

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:58.070
message of the film as any other,

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:00.140
intended to tell the viewer that the

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.660
economic might of Nazi Germany is so

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.899
great that even their propaganda is

00:12:05.899 --> 00:12:07.550
casually one of the most expensive

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:10.310
productions to date. every visual

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.560
implication of wealth strength and power

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.570
is made and then repeated and repeated

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:17.779
and repeated. Hitler descend from the

00:12:17.779 --> 00:12:20.360
majesty of the heaven. the old and

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:22.250
weathered architecture of Nuremberg is

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:24.740
peppered with Nazi icons, tying the new

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.720
regime to the perceived wealth and

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:29.750
stability of ages past. children gaze in

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:32.510
awe their glorious humble leader, a man

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:35.089
so blessed by the gods that even cats

00:12:35.089 --> 00:12:37.580
take notice of his passing. the Reich

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.560
is juxtaposed with churches, with the

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:42.110
pastoral calm of the rising sun, with

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:45.140
efficiency, with a bounty of food, and, of

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:47.720
course, with an endless supply of

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:50.990
soldiers. troops march and march and

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:54.140
march and march. the Nazi army does not

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.050
merely exist it goes on and on and on

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:59.540
and then on a little more after that.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.459
now there is no arc to the film because

00:13:01.459 --> 00:13:02.750
there is no conflict.

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:04.970
"look at us we're amazing." there is no

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.130
story, there is only message.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:09.290
oh it's mostly lies by the way

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:11.300
internally the Nazis were a mess. They

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:13.339
had after all just assassinated a number

00:13:13.339 --> 00:13:15.410
of their own high-ranking officers and

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:17.960
the army, which outnumbered the SA and

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:20.180
SS, was still very much on the fence

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:21.350
about their support for the regime

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:23.060
following the death of Hindenburg.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:24.950
Germany was still very much at risk of

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.600
tipping into a civil war between the

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:28.040
Nazis in the Wehrmacht.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.570
the whole point of the rally was to make

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:31.490
the film and the whole point of the film

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.050
was to project an image of an

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.480
unstoppable overwhelming wealthy happy

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:38.540
fed and unified Nazi Germany to

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.700
demoralize opponents and embolden

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:42.650
supporters. in fact there's a message

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:43.910
back there that you probably wouldn't

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.650
even catch, that whole thing about the

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:47.960
army. the actual german army, the Wehrmacht,

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:50.390
is barely in the film. there's one

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:52.370
scene of cavalry being inspected but

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:53.600
that's about it.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:54.980
all the rest of that endless sea of

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.440
troops are SA and SS troops which were

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.690
organs of the Nazi Party not of the

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.510
Armed Forces. it is a conscious exclusion

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:03.950
meant to establish a pecking order

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:06.110
between the Nazis and the Wehrmacht, to

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.300
make the potentially disloyal members of

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:10.490
the army feel small overwhelmed

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:13.130
unimportant and outnumbered. Throughout

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:15.350
the film the odious aspects of the Nazi

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:17.810
ideology, the concentration camps which

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.760
had already been operating for a year by

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:22.400
that point, the political assassinations,

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:23.390
the racism,

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:25.400
these are all downplayed or absent, left

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.830
unstated. the message is clear and

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.750
singular we are strong and prosperous

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:32.210
and anything we choose to do is

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:34.670
justified because it works and religious

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.860
imagery has been tapped to consecrate

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:39.800
that justification with divine favour.

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:41.540
historically this is also where we start

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:43.220
to really see the public beginning of

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:45.710
Nazi paganism with a parade of Nazi

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.050
flags being ceremonially consecrated by

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:50.480
touching them to the Blutfahn, a flag

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.070
that they claim had been carried by the

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:54.120
Nazis killed during the beer hall putsch.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.510
Now the relationship between the Nazis

00:14:56.510 --> 00:14:59.120
and religion is super complex and

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.940
interesting and you should definitely look into it

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:03.770
lots of books out there on the subject

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.660
but if you can get your hands on a copy

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:09.470
definitely check out the Urania's Children it's a really interesting short

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.420
read about astrology that's been out of

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:15.100
print for decades and The Occult Roots of Nazism.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:18.300
The short of it is that Nazism was a theological goulash.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:20.810
They made heavy use of Christian symbology and

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.370
tried to turn the numerous German

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:24.170
churches into an organ of the party

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:26.390
through the Confessional Church, but this

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:28.310
was largely a means to an end.

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:30.440
they didn't tap into Christian imagery

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:31.790
because they shared Christian values,

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:33.920
they did it because those images have

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:36.020
emotional meaning to the people.

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:38.060
simultaneously to this they were

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:39.860
co-opting any religious symbols that

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.720
they felt supported their own claim to

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:44.060
power, adopting the disparate trappings

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:46.200
of both Odinism and Hinduism.

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.170
This goes just as well for their approach to

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:52.279
science and their embrace of pseudoscience: it doesn't matter what

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:56.260
form it comes in as long as it reaches the desired conclusion.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:16:00.680
In the words of Hannah Arendt science is only a surrogate for power.

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:03.620
This is actually important: one of the main mechanisms of

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.660
propaganda is to plant the idea of

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:08.420
precedence, to alter the audience's own

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:10.790
sense of history and the world and

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:12.620
appeal to the seemingly objective

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:15.170
authorities of God, History, and Science.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:17.390
one of the most common use of propaganda

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:19.880
is to make new institutions seem much

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.740
older than they really are

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:23.960
by injecting themselves and their ideas

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:28.400
into history, what Umberto Eco described as a cult of tradition.

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:33.050
Nazi architecture is monumental in design, evocative of classical Greek and Roman.

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:37.850
Triumph of the Will places the new Nazi Party alongside centuries-old churches

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:43.280
Nazi eschatology dredges up old Norse runes to suggest an unbroken pure

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:45.840
lineage between the ancient &amp; the present.

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:51.220
Nazi pseudoscience says that the murder of Jews and Roma is acceptable because of blood.

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:55.240
The point of it all is to center the party in every aspect of life,

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.940
to make the party the mouthpiece of the gods.

00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:00.560
this is why there's all that bunk about

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:02.120
Riefenstahl being a visionary director

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.819
the legacy of Triumph of the Will is

00:17:04.819 --> 00:17:07.540
muddled because it was intentionally muddled.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.240
The party was trying to inject itself into everything,

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.500
into history, into art, into religion.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.319
They made their own movie and had their own critics praise

00:17:15.319 --> 00:17:17.329
it, to make it important.

00:17:17.329 --> 00:17:19.459
despite being funded entirely by the

00:17:19.459 --> 00:17:20.959
government, Triumph of the Will was

00:17:20.959 --> 00:17:23.120
released commercially, to distance it

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.819
from the party just enough to add a

00:17:25.819 --> 00:17:28.400
patina of legitimacy, to suggest that

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.410
Riefenstahl had captured something

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:34.490
unique and organic. And it worked.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:37.340
To this day we continue to use Triumph

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:39.170
of the Will as our reference point for

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:41.390
the mental construct of the Nazi regime.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:43.980
Which I want you to think about that.

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:46.460
Our idea of the Nazis is deeply

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.640
informed by a propaganda film produced

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:52.670
by the Nazis for the explicit purpose of

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.700
creating that mental construct.

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:59.120
This right here is exactly the image they

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:03.970
wanted you to think of when you thought of them.

